{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}k+9 \\\\ 2k+18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k+9=0 \\\\ 2k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-9.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2632da015634fd48c56296910dc0130953de22e06109c7d5ec72aca28e88c36f"} {"question" "q-34332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -12 & 4 \\\\ 9 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -12 & 4 \\\\ 9 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3k+6 \\\\ -12k-24 \\\\ 9k+18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3k+6=0 \\\\ -12k-24=0 \\\\ 9k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2632da015634fd48c56296910dc0130953de22e06109c7d5ec72aca28e88c36f"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34386" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2632da015634fd48c56296910dc0130953de22e06109c7d5ec72aca28e88c36f"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-34392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -12 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -12 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k-4 \\\\ 8k+16\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2k-4=0 \\\\ 8k+16=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2632da015634fd48c56296910dc0130953de22e06109c7d5ec72aca28e88c36f"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2632da015634fd48c56296910dc0130953de22e06109c7d5ec72aca28e88c36f"} {"question" "q-111220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072429/state.json" "file_sha256" "6733981ccadc3768cddb0401877004cbf6272c61672e79b57a5fc711214fac00"} {"question" "q-111220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] ["math" "{[\\beg